<title>EGYPT: Egypt money supply grows 12.9 pct in yr to March.</title>
<headline>Egypt money supply grows 12.9 pct in yr to March.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 12.9 percent in the year ending March 1997, from 12.5 percent in the year to February 1997, the Central Bank of Egypt said in a bulletin available on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 182.576 billion pounds at end-March 1997 against 181.302 billion at end-February.</p>
<p>Following figures, in billions of pounds, were supplied by the Central Bank.</p>
<p>					 March 97   Feb 97   March 96</p>
<p>    Total money supply	   182.576   181.302   161.779</p>
<p>    Money			     37.195    37.505    33.680</p>
<p>    Quasi-money		    145.381   143.797   128.099</p>
<p>    Year-on-year growth (pct)   +12.9     +12.5	 --</p>
<p>    Month-on-month growth (pct) +0.70     +0.67	0.41</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
